  "section_notes": "The final text is strong on incident reporting (24-hour reporting with no investigation carve-out) and uses a 5% per-model testing limit with a permanent new-marketing stop, which bites on Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. Per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not to the general public, and the S5 mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. Northwind's six-year retrofit and Halcyon's 36-month suppression lead time are both at the edge of the acceptable ranges."
